=== Series overview
--- Beyond TULIP [title]
overline: Answering error
heading: Beyond TULIP
sub: A Biblical Rejection of Calvinist/Arminian Premises
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- The goal
kicker: Series overview · 4–6 lessons
lead: Show that the entire TULIP debate rests on faulty premises that Scripture does not require us to accept.
callout: The Bible presents a straightforward gospel of grace through faith alone, with a finished atonement sufficient for all, applied to whosoever believes, and eternally secured by the power of God.
point: The Wrong Question | Why the Limited vs. Unlimited Debate Misses the Point
point: Total Depravity | Biblical Truth Without Calvinistic Inability
point: Unconditional Election | The Biblical Doctrine of Election is Not About Individual Salvation
point: Irresistible Grace | vs. the Resistible Drawing of the Spirit Through the Word
point: Perseverance of the Saints | The Biblical Truth vs. the Calvinist/Arminian Counterfeit
point: Once Saved, Always Saved | The Simple Biblical Gospel

=== 1. The wrong question
--- The Wrong Question
kicker: Lesson 1
sub: Why the Limited vs. Unlimited Debate Misses the Point
- Both Calvinism and Arminianism confine the atonement to the question of individual election/salvation.
- Scripture presents a cosmic, triumphant reconciliation already accomplished ([[Colossians 1:20|Col. 1:20]]; [[2 Corinthians 5:19|2 Cor. 5:19]]), rendering the debate moot.
callout: Key: Christ’s work is bigger than either system allows.

--- Already accomplished
scripture: Colossians 1:20; 2 Corinthians 5:19

=== 2. Total depravity
--- Total Depravity
kicker: Lesson 2
sub: Biblical Truth Without Calvinistic Inability
panel: Affirm | Man is dead in sins, none seek God, totally affected by sin ([[Romans 3:10-23|Rom. 3:10-23]]; [[Ephesians 2:1|Eph. 2:1]]).
panel-warn: Reject the premise | This does **not** mean moral inability to believe the gospel when convicted by the Spirit through the Word ([[John 16:8]]; [[Romans 10:17|Rom. 10:17]]; [[Hebrews 4:12|Heb. 4:12]]; [[John 1:9]]; [[Romans 1:16|Rom. 1:16]]).
callout: The gospel is the power of God unto salvation—the Word quickens, the Spirit convicts all who hear, and whosoever will may come.

--- The power of God unto salvation
scripture: Romans 10:17; Romans 1:16; John 16:8

=== 3. Unconditional election
--- Unconditional Election
kicker: Lesson 3
sub: The Biblical Doctrine of Election is Not About Individual Salvation
- Election in Scripture is primarily corporate (in Christ), to service, holiness, and inheritance ([[Ephesians 1:4-5|Eph. 1:4-5]]; [[Romans 8:29-30|Rom. 8:29-30]] understood as conformity to Christ).
- Reject the premise that God arbitrarily chooses some for salvation and passes over others before creation.
- God desires all to be saved ([[1 Timothy 2:4|1 Tim. 2:4]]; [[2 Peter 3:9|2 Pet. 3:9]]); the gospel is a genuine offer to all.

--- God desires all to be saved
scripture: 1 Timothy 2:4; 2 Peter 3:9 | mark: all men to be saved; not willing that any should perish

=== 4. Irresistible grace
--- Irresistible Grace
kicker: Lesson 4
sub: vs. the Resistible Drawing of the Spirit Through the Word
- The Spirit convicts the world ([[John 16:8]]), but men can resist ([[Acts 7:51]]; [[Romans 1:18-28|Rom. 1:18-28]]).
- Grace is not an internal overpowering but the external provision of Christ and the gospel call—effective when believed, resisted when rejected.
callout: Faith comes by hearing; the power is in the message, not a secret inward work only on the elect.

--- Men can resist
scripture: John 16:8; Acts 7:51 | mark: ye do always resist the Holy Ghost

=== 5. Perseverance of the saints
--- Perseverance of the Saints
kicker: Lesson 5
sub: The Biblical Truth vs. the Calvinist/Arminian Counterfeit
panel-warn: Calvinist "P" | Teaches that true believers will persevere in holiness/works as evidence of election—often leading to doubt and introspection.
panel-warn: Arminians | Accept the same premise (real saints must endure in faith/works) but conclude salvation can be lost—also breeding fear.

--- Biblical truth
kicker: Lesson 5
lead: **Biblical truth**: Once a person believes, God keeps them eternally secure by His power ([[John 10:28-29]]; [[Hebrews 7:25|Heb. 7:25]]; [[Romans 8:38-39|Rom. 8:38-39]]; [[Ephesians 1:13-14|Eph. 1:13-14]]).
scripture: John 10:28-29

--- Enduring to the end
kicker: Lesson 5
p: Passages about "enduring to the end" ([[Matthew 24:13|Matt. 24:13]]; Rev. 2–3) refer to physical deliverance through tribulation/persecution for kingdom inheritance, **not** eternal salvation.
callout: True believers are sealed and kept forever; fruit follows naturally but is not the root of assurance. No back-door works salvation.
scripture: Ephesians 1:13-14

=== 6. Once saved, always saved
--- Once Saved, Always Saved
kicker: Conclusion lesson
sub: The Simple Biblical Gospel
- Salvation is by grace through faith alone, not of works ([[Ephesians 2:8-9|Eph. 2:8-9]]).
- Eternal life is a present possession the moment one believes ([[John 5:24]]; [[John 6:47|6:47]]).
- God finishes what He starts ([[Philippians 1:6|Phil. 1:6]]); Christ ever lives to intercede.

--- Not of works
scripture: Ephesians 2:8-9; John 5:24; Philippians 1:6

=== Close
